WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
Late 1943.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.550
A writer begins typing a
short book about a farm,

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.330
and a group of pigs.

4
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.760
The manuscript goes to a publisher.

5
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.190
The door closes.

6
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.290
Another door.

7
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.300
Another.

8
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.550
Another.

9
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.760
In June 1944 a bomb
hits the writer's flat.

10
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.280
The pages scatter, but
the manuscript is rescued.

11
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.650
It finally comes out on 17 August 1945.

12
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.400
So why would wartime publishers
turn down a story about pigs?

13
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.920
In this mission, you'll go back to Russia,

14
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.770
from the revolution of
1917 to Stalin's rule.

15
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.120
You'll see how the farm's story
maps onto that history, loosely.

16
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.960
And you'll follow the
manuscript from door to door,

17
00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.400
until one finally opens.

18
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.660
Your mission: explain why wartime
publishers turned it down.
